	(text "Set-point and hardware CV: V_SET divider, protective pull-downs, CV error amplifier"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 22.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 4.5 4.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "394341d7-5c6a-5356-9e5a-21fa31719e79")
	)
	(text "V_SET = LOAD_CTRL / 16 is the only node the four channels follow. Anything that must stop the load pulls it to AGND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 26.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "54056533-903c-5dce-ae56-43a1c8d3e273")
	)
	(text "R31 / R32 = 15 : 1, 1 % (the gain is calibrated): 4.096 V in gives 256 mV = 2.56 A per channel. C33 slews the\nstep in 9 us so the loops never see a step edge. Q11 and Q12 are hardware and work with\nthe MCU dead. CV (block B) pulls this node down too, so LOAD_CTRL stays the ceiling in CV."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.61 93.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "141939ea-1321-584b-8771-ded585165466")
	)
	(text "A   V_SET: 0 - 256 mV = 0 - 10.24 A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.31 42.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e8eb3b63-4daa-52f1-b454-35d284164d07")
	)
	(text "spare section: follower at AGND"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 294.61 154.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e05eefaa-1699-543c-9f34-e34a5467cac8")
	)
	(text "Why: a current-source DUT cannot be held in CC (two current sources in series rail to\ncompliance), and a firmware CV loop on the DAC cannot either: 1 LSB into the 2.2 uF snubber\nslews 11 V in one 10 ms update. Here: V_DUT below CV_SET -> U12C rises -> Q13 pulls V_SET\ndown -> less current. CV_SET = 0 V: VSEN_OA (85 mV minimum) > CV_SET, U12C stays low, Q13\noff, plain CC (decks 01-04). Deck 06: settles for 0.1 - 8 A with and without 47 uF across\nthe DUT. Below 0.1 A it hunts: use CC or a resistor there."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.61 193.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2ea3644b-7c71-52fd-af02-e759cbd888bd")
	)
	(text "B   Hardware constant-voltage loop (LTspice rev_e deck 06)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.85 115.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3131708a-8686-57c0-affd-35e4da4d6223")
	)
	(text "Same nets, second names: VSET_MON feeds the ADC read-back (page 6), VSEN_OA_OVP hands the VSEN amplifier\noutput on to the over-voltage comparator (page 9). They exist so the top sheet can be drawn as a block diagram\nwith wires, without a net label."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 138.61 231.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "77cf7a98-7375-5284-8737-87c9bbac81f8")
	)
